ement of the background.\n\n[Shot 1]\nThe actress initially looks down at her smartphone, calmly scrolling with both hands. A handheld microphone slowly enters the frame from the lower left, held by an off-camera male interviewer. She notices the microphone, stops using the phone, gently lowers it onto her lap, and raises her eyes toward the interviewer.\n\nThe male interviewer asks in a friendly and professional Japanese voice:\n\n「お疲れさまです。今日の撮影はいかがでしたか？」\n\nThe actress listens attentively, gives a small polite nod, then smiles naturally and answers in Japanese:\n\n「とても楽しかったです。皆さんのおかげで、いい作品になりそうです。」\n\nWhile speaking, her expression gradually brightens. She maintains eye contact with the off-camera interviewer, makes one subtle hand gesture near the phone, and finishes with a gentle nod and a warm smile. Her blinking, breathing, lip movement, cheek movement, and posture changes remain subtle and realistic. The phone stays securely on her lap. The microphone remains close to her without touching her.\n\nCamera:\nA single continuous medium shot based on the reference composition. Begin with the same slightly tilted handheld framing. The camera makes a slow, restrained push-in after the microphone enters, moving from a medium shot toward a slightly closer portrait framing. Preserve the actress’s position on the right side of the frame and the visible white sofa on the left. Use mild natural handheld movement, realistic autofocus adjustment when she raises her head, shallow depth of field, and stable spatial continuity. Avoid sudden cuts, dramatic reframing, exaggerated gestures, facial distortion, identity drift, costume changes, or polished commercial camera movement.\n\nAudio:\nSpoken language is Japanese. The interviewer is an adult Japanese male with a calm, friendly off-camera voice. The actress speaks with a natural young Japanese female voice, warm and slightly tired after filming. Use accurate Japanese lip synchronization and clear turn-taking with no overlapp